 :record/cljs-tail "249 repos and 567 files whose only residual is .cljs. 225 have no project file of any kind, and the 224 distinct names among those are NAMED BY NOBODY: measured across all four ways this workspace wires a dependency -- a git coordinate in a deps.edn or bb.edn (619 names), a :local/root (375 names), a cross-repo :source-paths entry in a shadow-cljs.edn (122 path segments), and an npm script's --classpath (47 names). Zero matches on each. The measurement carries its own controls: kotoba-lang/text and kotoba-lang/json are both present in the consumed set and an invented name is absent. So this is source that nothing compiles and nothing depends on; migrating it would change no behaviour anywhere, and there is nowhere to declare the dependency."
 :record/repairs "Four deps.edn files were still split in half on main by the migration tool's pre-2026-09-08 insertion arithmetic -- cloud-itonami/ainori, kotoba-lang/capability-http-fetch, capability-llm-infer, capability-mmio-map. All four failed clojure -Stree with exit 1 and now exit 0. A fifth, network-awai/app-tabi-mikake, was broken BEFORE the migration by an unclosed vector in its :lint alias; checked at the pre-migration commit before being repaired, because the migration had also edited that file and the obvious guess was wrong. The earlier claim that all 29 corrupted files had been repaired was the number found, not the number that existed: that pass read local checkouts, which are routinely behind."
 :record/tool-changes "Two, both on com-junkawasaki/root main. (1) A file's require list can live outside an ns form: nine files keep a top-level (require ...) and were refused as having nowhere to declare the dependency, which held three repos and 104 files. (2) The tool now checks the project file it writes, not only the source it rewrites: read both sides and require that everything outside :deps is identical and that :deps differs by exactly one entry. A first version checking only that the result PARSED was discriminated as insufficient -- reintroducing the bug at a different offset produced an even number of forms, a clean parse, and :deps bound to a symbol."
 :record/unresolved "17 of the 348 never-merged repos could not be measured at all -- 12 have no local checkout, 5 have no remote matching their path. UNRESOLVED, which is not clean."
